        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9758/3 Follicular dendritic cell sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 361,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55738,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B31.5 Follicular dendritic cell sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 362,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55739,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> follicular dendritic cell tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 363,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55740,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 364,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55741,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FDC sarcoma can occur in nodal or extranodal sites. In a literature review of 343&nbsp;reported cases of FDC sarcoma, the liver was involved in 45&nbsp;cases (with EBV-positive inflammatory FDC sarcoma probably accounting for a high proportion), the GI tract in 18&nbsp;cases, and the pancreas in 5&nbsp;cases {23755890}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 365,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55742,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually present with a mass lesion in the involved organ. Rare patients have paraneoplastic pemphigus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 366,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55743,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FDC sarcoma is rare. The patients are usually adults, and there is no sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 367,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55744,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 368,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55745,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A proportion of cases have been reported to show IG gene rearrangement, a finding that requires further studies in light of the postulated mesenchymal derivation of normal FDCs {19145200}. EBV is negative, in contrast to the consistent EBV positivity in EBV-positive inflammatory FDC sarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 375,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 207,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55746,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 207,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FDC sarcomas are soft, bulky tumour masses.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 369,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55747,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 169,
        "headingText": "<p>The tumour comprises spindly to ovoid cells forming fascicles, storiform arrays, whorls, diffuse sheets, and vague nodules. The tumour cells show indistinct cell borders and a moderate amount of eosinophilic cytoplasm. The oval or elongated nuclei often show delicate nuclear membranes, vesicular chromatin, and distinct nucleoli, with variable degrees of pleomorphism. Binucleated and multinucleated forms are common. The tumour is typically lightly infiltrated by small lymphocytes, which can be aggregated around the blood vessels. FDC sarcoma shows immunoreactivity for one or more FDC markers, such as CD21, CD23, CD35, CXCL13, FDC-secreted protein, and serglycin {12121233; 28145886}. PDL1 is often positive {28130401}. Variable staining for EMA, S100, and CD68 can be present, whereas cytokeratin, CD1a, langerin, lysozyme, and myeloperoxidase are negative.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-23T16:40:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 370,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55748,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 371,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55749,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 374,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55750,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> spindly to oval cell neoplasm with storiform, fascicular, or whorled growth pattern; neoplastic cells show indistinct cell borders, vesicular nuclei, and distinct nucleoli; sprinkling of small lymphocytes; positive immunostaining for one or more FDC markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 372,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55751,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 373,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55752,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FDC sarcoma is a low-grade to intermediate-grade malignancy. A pooled analysis of the literature shows local recurrence and distant metastasis rates of 28% and 27%, respectively {23755890}. Large tumour size (&ge;&nbsp;6&nbsp;cm), coagulative necrosis, high mitotic count, and substantial cytological atypia are associated with a worse prognosis {23755890; 9010103}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:40:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]